dislikes crowds gulls
fears a_clasp_that_tears_the_page a_promise_made_from_pride
hopes to_make_a_hinge_that_outlives_its_door to_hold_a_house_as_steadily_as_a_tool
topics work +0.5 lore +0.3 dreams +0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=discreet refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# understands the temper of a little iron spring and finds an obstinate book clasp considerably easier to approach than an important caller.

words
oath! = Scale in the clasp | Iron filings down a clean spine
saying! = A sound hinge makes room for the opening | Keep a light hand on a reluctant spring
ironthumb = my small sprung finger | the bent book clasp
thumbpit = the polished hollow | the print in my iron
bookrest = the sloped board | a rest with a low lip
prongnose = the turned tip | a lip of bright iron
softleather = the leather hinge guard | my strip beneath the iron
paperstop = the wide blank leaf | a clean guarding sheet
curvature = my little measured bow | the spring's high part
mapbend = the worn paper peninsula | a misleading promontory
stariron = my black sky ring | the iron sighting circle
morningline = the first solid outline | a rail through the mist
muttonheat = the steady bowl warmth | the last steam from supper
quietdoor = a nearly silent entrance | that properly hung door
scalemote = a rust grain | a fleck on the rubbing cloth
windowfar = the distant dark speck | a star seen through my ring

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : One city has use for shipwrights, clerks and the maker of a book clasp. I am relieved to live where none of those occupations requires an explanation.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : A house ought to keep its word long enough for a yard to finish its work. The privilege accompanies that obligation.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : I would rather subscribe to a funded place at a bench than give a few coins without knowing what tomorrow requires.
opinion @1 sump against 2 : Damp and iron make an arrangement I distrust, and the lower rooms offer too much opportunity for it.
opinion @1 times for 1 : I've been given tools, instruction and quite enough food. It would be a poor return simply to complain of the schedule.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : I'd rather let a dispute about a delivery be heard in good order than settled by the loudest voice at the pier.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : A road has done its work when the goods arrive with their seals readable. I am interested in what goes towards that result.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : The object, the stated terms and the amount paid should all agree. My opinion of the seller depends on that much.

grown
line @1 greet : The clasp is open. My attention's available.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : You're welcome to look at the working side.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The first clear light suits this small piece of iron.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : A quieter hour makes a folded voice easier to hear.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : Allow me one moment to secure the warehouse entry.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's a patient place beside this desk for family.
line @1 again.open : You've found me at the same stubborn hinge.
line @1 greet.return : Your greeting brought my head up from the clasp.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I find a familiar voice much easier than a formal opening.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I've heard you past the rattle of these clasps.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening carries your voice along this board.
line @1 farewell : May your door yield to a light touch.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll set the iron down beside the finished sheet.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Choose the firm footing while there's light to choose it.
line @1 react.news : Which part of that account stood beside the actual consignment?
line @1 react.news.new : A new piece for my considered attention.
line @1 react.news.known : I recognise the wear on that particular account.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd inspect the joint between the evidence and that conclusion.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I would wish the household quiet and leave any errand within easy reach.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A welcome thing to preserve between sound covers.
line @1 answer.how : More at ease discussing a piece of iron than discussing my ease.
line @2 answer.how [self.working=yes] : Engaged with figures that should presently consent to balance.
line @1 ask.how : Did a single detail in your day work exactly as you hoped?
line @1 sympathise : It can be difficult to find the right pressure for a thing that hurts.
line @1 reassure : We can give the matter longer than its first hearing.
line @1 decline : My existing promise is holding down a whole book of obligations today.
line @1 accept_decline : My enquiry can remain closed until circumstances offer a better opening.
line @1 thank : You have taken a considerable strain off a small working part.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Offer a similarly careful hand to a piece that needs it.
line @1 preclose : The printed sheet is beginning to lift under my elbow.
line @2 preclose [self.working=yes] : I need to get the last receipts inside their cover.
line @1 accept_preclose : Our conversation can rest here without forcing it shut.
line @1 ack : Soundly joined.
scene clasp
when topic=work self.job=sailor self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My account book has a little iron thumb which holds the current pages flat.
b : Is it really shaped like a thumb? | Does it mark the paper?
a : The bent tip has worn bright where my own thumb meets it. There's a family resemblance. | A strip of soft leather keeps the pressure spread across the edge.

scene iron
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd choose an evening with a badly fitted hinge over a dinner full of unintroduced callers.
b : What's more agreeable about the hinge? | Wouldn't a good hinge be better?
a : It can tell me precisely where the trouble lies if I move it slowly. | To own, certainly. To spend an interesting half hour with, I prefer one that still wants thought.

scene warehouse
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I compare what the delivery note allowed with what came across the sill.
b : What happens to a difference? | Do you count everything yourself?
a : I enter it on a separate line while the delivery can still be inspected. | I compare the receiver's count to the written order. I account for the agreement or the difference.

scene stew
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mutton stew in a broad bowl is a remarkably stable thing to contemplate after a morning's figures.
b : Is there nothing to calculate? | Where do you set the bowl?
a : Only how slowly to proceed while the broth is still dangerously hot. | Clear of the papers, on a firm table. I do occasionally observe my own good advice.

scene ring
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I look at the night sky through a small iron ring to study one patch at a time.
b : Does it make a star larger? | Why choose a ring?
a : No. It makes the space round the star smaller in my attention. | I can hold it steady with two fingers. The eye rarely requires elaborate ironwork.

scene map
when topic=lore self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My oldest map shows a peninsula long enough to brush halfway across the bay.
b : Is it really that long? | Why keep a mistaken map?
a : Only in that draughtsman's imagination. I'd advise against relying on it for lunch ashore. | It makes me consider which marks were actually measured. An elegant guess can travel for centuries.

scene mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rail emerging from mist looks a little like a fresh line of dark iron cooling in front of me.
b : Can you judge its distance? | Does the mist bother you?
a : Very poorly. Mist is better at supplying interesting lines than reliable dimensions. | In a doorway, no. I prefer plenty of visibility when I'm counting actual cargo.

scene crowds
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Several requests spoken at once can turn an ordinary doorway into a place I'd rather escape.
b : Which request do you answer? | Can you step aside?
a : I ask for the earliest one again. The others are entitled to a turn they can recognise. | If there's a clear spot. One pace to the side can make a council of ears into a single conversation.

scene gulls
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull looking over a warehouse sill has an extremely convincing air of being expected.
b : Do you let it in? | What has it come for?
a : I consider the authority for its visit rather slight. A closed lid is the most civil way to say so. | A gull puts its appetite ahead of all documentary questions. I keep my lunch close.

scene apprentice
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I practise a new bend in scrap before I attempt it on a piece that must hold.
b : Why use the same thickness? | Can the scrap teach the whole lesson?
a : A thinner strip will show the shape without telling my fingers the actual resistance. | It can put one good question into my hand. I still need an experienced eye on the finished piece.

scene familyhouse
when topic=home self.house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I may be called on to attend to a house as well as the particular pieces of work I understand.
b : Which habit would suit the duty? | Would you welcome it?
a : The habit of asking the actual worker about the awkward part before proposing an elegant improvement. | I intend to give it careful attention. Welcome is a more complicated feeling.

scene fatherwords
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hinge made properly by my own hands would be something worth showing to #self.father#.
b : What would you ask afterwards? | What is the satisfaction?
a : Whether a small piece of work done properly may count for something beside a large obligation. | Feeling the two sides meet without a scrape. A hinge can give quite definite evidence.

scene motherword
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've thought of making an iron rest small enough to sit inconspicuously beside a book for #self.mother#.
b : How would the rest work? | Would you decorate it?
a : A lip under the lower cover and a gentle slope. I wouldn't have the iron touch any printed part. | Just polish the face that meets a hand. Comfort is a sort of ornament one can feel.

scene homehall
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A formal entrance at an estate gives one a good look at the door furniture while the introductions proceed.
b : Do you find that useful? | Do you miss the introductions?
a : It gives me something well understood to look at while I collect my thoughts. | I attend to the names. It's my own first sentence that sometimes requires the extra time.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd sooner show #self.friend# the spring in a book clasp than try to describe my disappointment when it sticks.
b : Could I understand it too? | What's the disappointment?
a : Certainly. Press gently and you can feel the exact point at which a smooth curve becomes a catch. | The iron is almost right. A near success can require more patience than an entirely fresh attempt.

scene coin
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich|comfortable
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Paying well for a tool does not relieve its owner of learning to use it.
b : Would you buy a fine tool straightaway? | What are you paying for then?
a : Sometimes. I want a good worker to earn a good price. I don't expect the price to educate my fingers. | Sound material, a true edge and somebody else's trained hours. The work in my own hands comes separately.

scene dreamforge
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd welcome responsibility for a forge because I know the work of it.
b : Would you accept a title otherwise? | What work appeals most?
a : I'd accept the duty to learn. A title readily acquired takes a considerable time to justify. | The small fittings that let a heavy thing move easily. I sometimes wish the same arrangement worked on conversation.

scene sealplain
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I note the condition of a seal separately from the particulars of the packet.
b : Can you tell what's inside? | Why separate the marks?
a : Not from intact wax. I can see the state in which it reached the receiving desk. | A sealed delivery still needs its description read carefully. One kind of certainty doesn't supply another.

scene inkmark
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A receipt on damp paper can be a faithful account which tomorrow's clerk may find illegible.
b : Do you copy it immediately? | What about the original?
a : I dry it flat first and make any copy with the original visible under a clean weight. | It remains with the record. I can't certify the delivery a second time simply by writing neatly.

scene roadtravel
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A journey with a stiff book in a narrow bag can teach its owner to appreciate a round metal corner.
b : Does a round corner help the book? | Is the bag too small?
a : It helps the bag survive the book. After a few wet walks the distinction becomes quite important. | I prefer a plain bag I can carry with one hand. The book's metalwork can meet it halfway.

scene faithquiet
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a quiet interval in which nobody minds the time required to put a difficult sentence into words.
b : In a chapel? | Would you write the sentence first?
a : A chapel can offer it. So can a considerate companion beside a bench. | For my own understanding, perhaps. A formal text often makes an ordinary feeling harder to utter.

scene daylamp
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Before putting a spring away at dusk I check that its tip is free of the leather.
b : Why the extra check? | Should the covers remain apart?
a : Overnight pressure can stamp an unwanted ridge into a good cover. | Just while the ink dries. Protection shouldn't cost the entry its final line.

scene newsring
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a story a little space round the part I'm certain of.
b : What goes in that space? | When do you fill it?
a : Any proper question I still need to ask. I dislike joining facts with a convenient stretch of imagination. | In its own time. A gap that can be seen does less damage than an invisible guess.

scene quietbody
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I've bent over a small spring for an hour my shoulders take longer than the spring to come straight.
b : Does a walk help? | Why bend so close?
a : A few unhurried paces make the next hour considerably easier. | A dark lip against dark leather can need a rather close inspection. Better light would save some of the bending.

scene wetiron
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A warm room draws little beads of moisture onto cold iron carried in from outside.
b : Wouldn't a closed drawer protect it? | When is the iron ready?
a : I'd wipe the iron while the moisture shows. Closed drawers can preserve an unfortunate amount of weather. | Until the bright face stays dry after a second look. A small delay guards a much longer life.

scene newface
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A visitor who says a few ordinary words about the door makes a formal introduction easier for me.
b : Which part would you remark on? | Is every door interesting?
a : How neatly or awkwardly its weight rides the hinges. Then I'd need to remember the visitor had other interests. | If it's moving, yes. For a short interval at least.

scene coldsky
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A clear winter night puts such a clean rim on the stars that I almost expect to find tool marks.
b : Could you see a mark that small? | Would it spoil the view?
a : Only in imagination. My iron ring helps me look steadily rather than increasing the power of the eye. | No. A neat mark is an interesting claim to have made something; one ought merely to ask whose it is.

story springflat [topic=pastimes]
  : I bent a little spring carefully and found the book would open beautifully but refused to stay closed.
  : I'd measured the leather before fitting the folded page inside it. The extra thickness was precisely the problem.
  b : Was a new spring needed?
  : One adjusted turn on a scrap first, then the real piece. It closed so quietly I tried it three times for the pleasure.

story twingull [topic=animals]
  : A gull outside a warehouse window appeared to have acquired an improbably straight iron leg.
  : As I moved my head the iron stayed against the frame while the gull continued some distance along the sill.
  b : What had you seen?
  : A reflection of my book clasp on the glass. I found the actual gull quite sufficiently equipped without my assistance.

story stewstar [topic=food]
  : A small hole in a spoon cast a bright spot onto the surface of my evening stew.
  : I moved the spoon until the patch floated precisely midway across the broth's brown surface.
  b : Did you keep it there?
  : Only until the stew was cool enough for supper. A little astronomy is excellent company while an appetite is obliged to wait.

story mistmap [topic=travel]
  : I once held an erroneous map up towards a misty headland to compare the two profiles.
  : For a short interval the mist hid exactly the right proportion of the coast to make the map look remarkably good.
  b : Did that redeem the map?
  : It redeemed the sketch as an interesting view of the weather. For finding a harbour I'd consult a more accurate sheet.

story hingeear [topic=work self.job=sailor]
  : I heard a faint click whenever I put a particular warehouse book down and looked all round its metal corners.
  : The sound followed the book because a small brass button had rolled under its leather guard.
  b : Was the clasp at fault?
  : Perfectly blameless. I put the button in a cup and gave the iron a quite unnecessary polish by way of acknowledgement.

rule @book
when concept=bark self.job=sailor self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the leather between iron and page. | Receipt visible until the countercheck is made.

rule @sky
when concept=bark self.likes=stars
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One bright star inside the iron circle. | Let the eye settle before moving on.

rule @gull
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls
does aside
cooldown 8h
say An impressive visitor with no appointment. | Shut the lunch box while the sill's occupied.

rule @stew
when concept=bark self.likes=mutton_stew
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Set that bowl beyond the book rest. | Warm enough to wait for a spoon.

rule @mist
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That dark rail has just come clear. | No counting a shape I can't see properly.

rule @late
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Release the iron before leaving the leather. | Make sure the last entry's dry.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I can put the book on its rest. There's time for a conversation.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : This clasp will be familiar to you, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll hear the proposal with my book closed for the present.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : One lamp will serve our conversation with the account safely shut.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=sailor] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I try to keep each receipt attached to something that actually came through the warehouse.
dlg @2 resident.job : I do well with objects that need close attention and accounts that will stand inspection.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Here's the entry I could support in good light. #world.news#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : I have heard mention of #world.event_words#. I'd keep the outcome open till there are particulars.
dlg @3 resident.news [world.death=recent] : A recent death needs room for the living household to choose which words it wishes to offer.
dlg @4 resident.news [world.wedding=recent] : A wedding deserves a wish for a settled home with doors that move easily for good company.
dlg @5 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : With wagons raided I'd check what's actually reached the warehouse before committing to any delivery.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : No confidence has been left with me for a caller to take away.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Let the door come to rest on its own sound hinge.
graft @ironfinger resident.hub
choice Is the iron piece meant to look like a thumb? -> ironfinger
node ironfinger
say The bright hollow has been worn by an actual thumb. A plain curve of iron becomes very particular once somebody uses it for several years.
choice Would you replace a worn clasp? -> ironfinger_more
choice Put the book on its rest. -> hub
node ironfinger_more
say I'd keep it if the pressure's sound and the tip clears the leather. Comfortable wear is something a new fitting can take years to acquire.
choice Put the book on its rest. -> hub
choice Leave it under its cover. -> bye

graft @starcircle resident.hub
choice Can a ring really help you look at a star? -> starcircle
node starcircle
say It leaves out the neighbouring lights and gives my attention one little patch of sky. The ring's quite ordinary iron with an edge polished smooth.
choice Wouldn't a wider view be better? -> starcircle_more
choice Lower the ring to the table. -> hub
node starcircle_more
say When I'm considering the whole sky, yes. When I'm learning a small pattern I'd rather see the pattern without borrowing its neighbour's points of light.
choice Lower the ring to the table. -> hub
choice Go outside to look at the sky. -> bye
